{"name":"Silver Charm","hex":"#adb0b4","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"silver","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A lustrous, white, metallic element, atomic number 47, atomic weight 107.87, symbol Ag.","Coins made from silver or any similar white metal."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made from silver.","Made from another white metal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silver"},{"term":"charm","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An object, act or words believed to have magic power (usually carries a positive connotation).","The ability to persuade, delight or arouse admiration."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To seduce, persuade or fascinate someone or something.","To use a magical charm upon; to subdue, control, or summon by incantation or supernatural influence; to ensorcel or exert a magical effect on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/charm"}],"entries":[{"title":"Silver Charm","blocks":[{"text":"Silver Charm is a champion American Thoroughbred racehorse who won the 1997 Kentucky Derby and Preakness Stakes and 1998 Dubai World Cup. He stood at stud in the United States and Japan, and is now retired at Old Friends Farm in Kentucky."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Silver_Charm_Old_Friends.jpg/330px-Silver_Charm_Old_Friends.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_Charm","wikidata":"Q7515889"},{"title":"Silver","blocks":[{"text":"Silver is a chemical element; it has symbol Ag and atomic number 47. A soft, white, lustrous transition metal, it exhibits the highest electrical conductivity, thermal conductivity and reflectivity of any metal. Silver is found in the Earth's crust in the pure, free elemental form, as an alloy with gold (electrum) and other metals, and in minerals such as acanthite, argentite and chlorargyrite. Most silver is recovered as a byproduct of lead–zinc, copper and gold mining and refining."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Silver_crystal.jpg/330px-Silver_crystal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver","wikidata":"Q1090"},{"title":"Silver (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Silver or metallic gray is a color tone resembling gray that is a representation of the color of polished silver."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Clemens_Friedell_silver_centerpiece_bowl_top_view_-_HLABG.png/330px-Clemens_Friedell_silver_centerpiece_bowl_top_view_-_HLABG.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_(color)","wikidata":"Q317802"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Silver_Charm_2.jpg/500px-Silver_Charm_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Silver_Charm_2.jpg/500px-Silver_Charm_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Silver Charm in Japan (2006)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASilver_Charm_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Silver_Charm_at_Old_Friends_fundraiser_-_5-5-24.jpg/500px-Silver_Charm_at_Old_Friends_fundraiser_-_5-5-24.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Silver_Charm_at_Old_Friends_fundraiser_-_5-5-24.jpg/1280px-Silver_Charm_at_Old_Friends_fundraiser_-_5-5-24.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Silver_Charm_at_Old_Friends_fundraiser_-_5-5-24.jpg/500px-Silver_Charm_at_Old_Friends_fundraiser_-_5-5-24.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=